{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-17010-r4519033","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Tomato Sauce Piquante","sourcePageId":17010,"sourceRevision":"4519033","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T17:20:29Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tomato%20Sauce%20Piquante&oldid=4519033","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:22.147Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Italian recipes","Category:Public domain recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for pasta sauce","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using bay leaf","Category:Recipes using broth and stock","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using ham","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using superfine sugar","Category:Recipes using tomato"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2e4784631236bb112ab7ab556e75b35a72f5fe72c42f301f96ee810eadd0f312","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{recipe summary|\n| category    = Italian recipes\n| servings    = 2\n| time        = 30 minutes\n| difficulty  = 2\n| energy      =\n| image       =\n}}\n{{recipe}}\n\n{{Decameron}}\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 ounce [[Cookbook:Ham|ham]]\n* [[Cookbook:Butter|Butter]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]]\n* ½ stalk [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Bay leaf|bay leaf]]\n* 1 sprig [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Clove|clove]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Pepper|peppercorns]]\n* ⅓ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]]\n* ½ glass [[Cookbook:Wine|Chablis white wine]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]]\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], cut up and strained of all their liquid\n* Veloute or [[Cookbook:Espagnole sauce|Espagnole sauce]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Castor sugar|castor sugar]]\n* Juice of ½ [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]]\n* 1 ounce butter\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Cut up the ham, onion, carrot, and celery very finely. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] them in butter together with the bay leaf, thyme, clove and peppercorns.\n# Over this pour the vinegar, and when the liquid is all absorbed, add the Chablis and stock, then the tomatoes.\n# Cook this in a covered stew pan and pass it through a [[Cookbook:Sieve|sieve]], making sure none of the bay leaf or thyme goes through.\n# Mix this sauce with an equal quantity of Veloute sauce (No. 2) or Espagnole sauce, (No. 1), let it [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] and pass through a sieve again.\n# Add the castor sugar, the lemon juice, and butter.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Another tomato sauce may be made like this, using stock instead of vinegar and leaving out the lemon juice and sugar.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Italian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pasta sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ham]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using superfine sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using broth and stock]]","isRecipe"